{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04HG", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$s$", "MATH_0003": "$\\{x_1, \\ldots, x_n\\}$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$W$", "MATH_0006": "$U$", "MATH_0007": "$X_U \\to U$", "MATH_0008": "$u$", "MATH_0009": "$U$", "MATH_0010": "$W = \\emptyset$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-unramified-etale-local-technical}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{morphisms-section-integral}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c461f9e84ba7d50f856d09a4dbffe090d8ef10f902edb1c77bf0281dbac283b3", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:958c943713a7544d27138294d63ae7cac2259cfb0d9103f752ec52eacca32748", "source_text": "Since <MATH_0001> is finite the fibre over <MATH_0002> is a finite set\n<MATH_0003> of points of <MATH_0004>. Apply\nLemma <REF_0001>\nto this set (a finite morphism is separated, see\nMorphisms, Section <REF_0002>).\nThe image of <MATH_0005> in <MATH_0006> is a closed\nsubset (as <MATH_0007> is finite, hence proper) which does not\ncontain <MATH_0008>. After removing this from <MATH_0009> we see that <MATH_0010>\nas desired.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3788088943448795ec0db9034c8525b44fa037586475873e65bccddcb9436cff", "unit_id": "tag:04HJ:proof"}
